msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:63
msgid "Reads a post's Yoast SEO fields from its post meta: title, description, focus keyword, canonical URL, the social tags, and the three robots directives (noindex, nofollow, and the advanced list). Requires edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:64
msgid "Reads the rendered Yoast SEO head markup for a post when it is available, and an empty string when it is not. Requires the edit-posts capability and edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:65
msgid "Reads a post's Rank Math SEO fields from its post meta: title, description, focus keyword, canonical URL, the social tags, and the robots directives. Requires edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:66
msgid "Reads a post's structured-data schema of a given type (for example Article or FAQPage) from Rank Math. Requires edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:67
msgid "Reads the rendered Rank Math SEO head markup for a post when it is available, and an empty string when it is not. Requires the edit-posts capability and edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:68
msgid "Reads a post's SEO fields from All in One SEO's own data store, not post meta: title, description, canonical URL, the social tags, and the noindex and nofollow flags. Requires edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:69
msgid "Reads the rendered All in One SEO head markup for a post when it is available, and an empty string when it is not. Requires the edit-posts capability and edit access to that post."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:70
msgid "Lists your ACF field groups and the fields inside each one (key, label, and type) so an agent can discover what fields exist. It returns structure only, never stored values. Requires the edit-posts capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:73
msgid "Reads all of a user's ACF field values, hydrated by field key. If a field stores an email address (a user_email-type field), the real address is returned under the integration disclaimer. Requires edit access to that user."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:74
msgid "Lists your WooCommerce products with their id, name, SKU, price, stock status, status, categories, and featured flag, and the total count. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:75
msgid "Reads one WooCommerce product by id: description, prices, stock, images, attributes, variation ids, and categories. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:76
msgid "Lists a variable product's variations by parent product id: each variation's id, parent id, SKU, price, stock status, and status, plus a total. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:77
msgid "Reads one product variation by id: parent id, prices, stock, description, image, and its chosen attribute values. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:78
msgid "Lists all global WooCommerce product attribute taxonomies: id, name, slug, type, sort order, and whether it has public archives. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:79
msgid "Lists WooCommerce orders with their id, number, status, total, currency, date, and customer id, plus a total count. List rows carry no billing or shipping details. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:80
msgid "Reads one WooCommerce order by id: line items, totals, status, dates, customer note, and the full customer billing address - including email and phone - and the shipping address. Customer PII (email, phone, full address) is returned under the Integrations security disclaimer and is always gated by the manage-WooCommerce capability. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:83
msgid "Reads a single WooCommerce order refund by refund id. Returns the refund amount, reason, and date. Reason text is returned verbatim under the Integrations security disclaimer. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:84
msgid "Lists WooCommerce customers with their id, email, name, username, order count, and total spent, plus a total count. Defaults to the customer role; pass role to target another role, or \"all\" for every role. The email is a customer's personal data and is returned under the Integrations security disclaimer. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:85
msgid "Reads one WooCommerce customer by id: email, the billing address (including phone), the shipping address, order count, total spent, and the registration date. The email, phone, and addresses are personal data, returned under the Integrations security disclaimer and gated by the manage-WooCommerce capability. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:86
msgid "Creates a new WooCommerce order from optional status, customer id, customer note, billing address, shipping address, and line items. Returns the full order shape including billing and shipping PII under the Integrations security disclaimer. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:87
msgid "Updates a WooCommerce order by id, changing only the fields you send. An empty request is a no-op success. Returns the full order shape including PII under the Integrations security disclaimer. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:88
msgid "Sets the status of a WooCommerce order by id. Returns the full order shape, including the customer billing and shipping PII, under the Integrations security disclaimer. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:89
msgid "Creates a WooCommerce customer from an email, name, username, and optional billing and shipping addresses. Returns the full customer record, including the email and addresses, under the Integrations security disclaimer. Creates a real WordPress user account, so it requires the create-users capability as well as the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:90
msgid "Updates a WooCommerce customer by id, changing only the fields you send. An empty request is a no-op success. Returns the full customer record, including PII, under the Integrations security disclaimer. Requires the manage-WooCommerce capability."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:93
msgid "Creates a new draft post. The agent drafts, a human publishes. It never goes live on its own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:94
msgid "Creates and publishes a post. Requires the publish capability, and respects force-draft if you turned it on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:95
msgid "Updates an existing post's fields by id. Publishing is gated separately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/disclosures.php:96
msgid "Finds and replaces literal text in a post's body and sanitizes the result. It edits only the content, never the status, and the change is reversible from the revision history."
msgstr ""

